# NEXUS Project .gitignore
# Version: 1.0.0 | Date: 2026-08-28 | Sprint: 112
#
# Ships to an adopter's project root as `.gitignore` (dist-manifest.txt FRESH directive).
# Covers the files NEXUS generates that are machine-local and must not be committed.
# Project-specific build artifacts go at the bottom, where the commented examples are.

# User-specific Claude Code settings — holds the CLAUDE_CODE_FILE_READ_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS
# setting that /nexus:setup writes. Per machine and per clone, never shared.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Runtime hint files written by the hooks and by boot. Regenerated every session;
# committing them produces churn in every checkpoint and conflicts on every pull.
.nexus/.context-window
.nexus/.context-cache
.nexus/.freshness-checked

# Binary deliverable backups — managed by /nexus-backup-optimization, not by git.
# Relevant for creative and mixed project types (docx, pptx, pdf, images).
.nexus/backups/

# Python caches, from the hooks' interpreter
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# OS artifacts
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Build artifacts — uncomment or extend for your project
# node_modules/
# dist/
# build/
# .venv/
